    duplicate_of: []  # 5c8b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5c8b
    pr_ref:  # 5c8b
    description: "The v9.1.0 release run (GitHub Actions run 38899828875, 2026-10-16) published to PyPI, then its \"Create GitHub Release\" step failed: `gh release create` got `HTTP 404: Not Found` from `uploads.github.com` while uploading `hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer-9.1.0.tar.gz`. The release https://github.com/iterabloom/hypergumbo/releases/tag/v9.1.0 exists and is not a draft, with 17 assets: 8 packages x (wheel + sdist) and SHA256SUMS. `dist/sbom.json` was generated (log: \"SBOM generated (78173 bytes)\") and is missing from the release. The workflow's own comment records v7.0.0 failing the same step with \"HTTP 400: Bad Content-Length\", so this is the second release left incomplete by a transient upload error.\n\nInvariant-shaped defect in `.github/workflows/release.yml` (not a governance file): asset upload has no retry and no completeness check, and a failure after `gh release create` leaves a published release missing assets with nothing to repair it.\n\nProposed fix: create the release first with no assets, then upload each asset with `gh release upload --clobber` in a retry loop (3 attempts, backoff), then verify `gh release view --json assets` lists every file in `dist/` and fail loudly if not. The retried upload is idempotent with `--clobber`, so a re-run of the job repairs a partial release instead of failing on \"already exists\".\n\nImmediate repair for v9.1.0: `gh release upload v9.1.0 dist/sbom.json` from a checkout that regenerates the SBOM, or accept its absence for that version. Owner's call."  # 5c8b
    fields: {}  # 5c8b
