- op: discuss  # 9196
  at: '2026-10-17T22:02:03Z'  # 9196
  by: agent  # 9196
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9196
  clock: 3  # 9196
  nonce: '9196'  # 9196
  message: "Fixed in PR #1697. Root cause: one gh release create <tag> <assets...> with no retry and no post-check, so one transient upload error (v7.0.0 HTTP 400, v9.1.0 HTTP 404) left a public Release incomplete; and the SBOM step inventoried the build env (v9.0.0 sbom.json: 66 components, no hypergumbo package). Fix: create the Release with no assets and only if absent; per-asset gh release upload --clobber with 4 attempts; verify attached names against the Release and fail naming gaps; SBOM built from the wheels installed into a scratch venv, dropped unless it contains hypergumbo-core, generated before SHA256SUMS. Behavioural evidence for the repair: v9.1.0 Release re-read via gh release view after the upload -> 18 assets, sbom.json 95,506 bytes, byte-identical (cmp) to the file generated from the release's own wheels (checksums verified against SHA256SUMS): 93 components incl. all 8 packages at release versions and 49 tree-sitter grammars. Not yet exercised: the rewritten workflow step itself runs only on the next tag push; its shape is pinned by tests/test_release_asset_upload.py. v9.1.0's SHA256SUMS predates sbom.json and was left as published."  # 9196
